# CODEOWNERS
#
# This file defines required reviewers for specific paths.
# GitHub enforces these reviews automatically on every PR.
# A listed owner must approve before the PR can merge, regardless
# of who else has approved.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Global fallback: all paths not matched below require a review from the
# core maintainers team. This prevents any file from having zero required
# reviewers, including new directories added in the future.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
* @kalviumcommunity/devops-instructors

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# src/payments.js — Financial transaction logic.
# Any change here carries direct monetary and compliance risk.
# The fintech-team owns correctness of all billing, tax, and payment
# calculations. A broken payment flow cannot be caught purely by tests;
# a domain expert must review for business-logic correctness.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/payments.js @kalviumcommunity/fintech-team

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# src/auth.js — Authentication and authorization.
# This file controls who can access the application and what they can do.
# Security vulnerabilities here (broken sessions, missing checks, JWT
# misuse) are critical. The security-team must review all changes.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/auth.js @kalviumcommunity/security-team

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# src/app.js — Application entry point and integration wiring.
# This file connects auth, payments, and all other subsystems.
# A change here can break cross-cutting concerns even when individual
# modules are untouched. Requires sign-off from both engineering leads.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
/src/app.js @kalviumcommunity/engineering-leads

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# .github/workflows/ — CI/CD pipeline definitions.
# Changes to workflow files control what runs in automated pipelines,
# including security scans, deployments, and branch protection checks.
# A developer could silently remove a required gate. Only the DevOps
# team may approve modifications to pipeline configuration.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/ @kalviumcommunity/devops-instructors

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# package.json — Dependency manifest.
# Adding, removing, or upgrading dependencies affects the supply chain.
# A compromised or outdated package can introduce CVEs into production.
# The security-team must approve all dependency changes.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
/package.json @kalviumcommunity/security-team
